{
 "name": "voice-message",
 "title": "Voice message",
 "description": "Dictate a message: tap the mic and the words appear in the message box while you speak (Mistral Voxtral Realtime, or local Whisper in short chunks), then a full pass corrects them when you stop. Never sends automatically and never overwrites your edits. Local Whisper runs on a GPU model or a small CPU model, so any machine works; its pinned Python runtime is built beside the module at first use (uv or python3-venv, faster-whisper and the small model from pinned revisions). The server holds the Mistral connection, and the key is read only on the server.",
